1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,500
Jjan (짠) — Korea's kye savings circle,
rebuilt on-chain.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In a traditional kye, one person holds the pot.
Organizers run off with it.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Here the contract holds it instead.
Zero admin drain paths.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,000
Connecting a wallet on GIWA Sepolia —
Upbit's OP Stack L2.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:24,000
The dashboard. Everything here is mock KRW
on testnet, not real funds.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:30,000
The built-in faucet mints 1,000,000 test
mKRW in a single click.

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Creating a circle: name it, then list the
member wallets in payout order.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Two wallets this run, M1 and M2.
The payout order is fixed right here.

9
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:49,000
100,000 mKRW per round, a 50,000 bond,
and a deliberately short round window.

10
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,500
One transaction: the factory clones
a brand-new Circle contract.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Created. Every circle is an EIP-1167 clone,
so deploying one costs almost nothing.

12
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,500
The circle: 200,000 mKRW pot per round,
two rounds, nobody joined yet.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
M1 approves mKRW once — enough for the bond
and every round after it.

14
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:19,000
Then joins by posting the 50,000 bond.
Collateral, slashed if you skip a round.

15
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:25,000
M1 is in — one of two joined.

16
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:31,000
Switching Rabby over to the second wallet, M2.

17
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:37,500
M2 approves the same one-time allowance.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
And joins, posting its own 50,000 bond.

19
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:51,000
Both bonds are now posted, and the contract
is the only thing holding them.

20
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:57,000
Two of two joined, so the circle can start.

21
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:03,000
Round 1 is live. The countdown is the round
window — nothing can close early.

22
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:10,000
Each member contributes 100,000 mKRW.
It lands in escrow, not in anyone's wallet.

23
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:17,000
Switching wallets to pay in from
the other side too.

24
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:24,000
Both contributions in. A 200,000 mKRW pot,
held by the contract alone.

25
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:30,000
Timer at zero. Every step is on GIWA's
Blockscout explorer as we go.

26
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:36,000
Now closeRound can be called — by anyone,
not just whoever created the circle.

27
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:43,000
closeRound succeeded. 200,000 mKRW paid
straight to round 1's scheduled member.

28
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:49,000
Confirmed in under a second on GIWA.
No one chose the recipient — the schedule did.

29
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:56,000
Round 2 of 2. The pot rotates to M2.

30
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:03,000
Same flow again: both members
pay in their 100,000.

31
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:10,000
The payout can't be redirected. It reads the
recipient fixed at creation, from storage.

32
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:17,000
Round 2 fully funded, window expired.

33
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:23,000
Closing the final round —
200,000 mKRW to M2 this time.

34
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:29,000
Circle finished. Each member took
exactly one pot, in the agreed order.

35
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:36,000
Now the bonds come back. Each member pulls
their own — the contract can't push it anywhere.

36
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:43,000
M1's 50,000 bond claimed.

37
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:50,000
M2 withdraws too. The circle is settled and
empty — every mKRW accounted for.

38
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:57,000
Every contribution, payout and withdrawal
is a verified event on the GIWA explorer.

39
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:02,500
The docs cover the architecture, the security
model, and the deployed contracts.

40
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,700
Fully bilingual, English and Korean.
Jjan — save with friends, trust no one.
